  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nThe aforementioned upper ridge over the Southwest U.S. will \nnudge further into the Pacific Northwest Friday through the \nweekend. Above normal temperatures will continue for SE Oregon \nand SW Idaho, climbing to the low-mid 80s for lower valleys. \nModels bring a weak disturbance across the forecast area late \nSunday and Monday, increasing cloud cover and precip chances. \nWhile NBM/WPC's probability of precipitation remains low during \nthis time, some ensemble members now indicate shower development\nacross southwest/central Idaho on Monday depending on moisture \navailability. Thereafter, the ridge should rebound on Tuesday, \nwith warm and dry conditions forecast.",
